<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="room-title">
  <div>
    <h2 id="room-title">
      A compact home for browser controls.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Keep the web in front.</h3><p>
        The resting island keeps navigation and tab controls in a slim band
        above the page. Open its panel for more controls without shifting the
        page below.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>See the essentials at a glance.</h3><p>
        At rest, the island shows the tabs in your current group as dots, the
        site you are on, and a quiet shield. Click the shield to see the
        connection and change Blanc Blocker for that site.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>It notices you coming.</h3><p>
        Move toward the island and it rises and grows a little, settling before
        you click and easing back as you leave. It follows how close you are
        rather than switching on at a threshold, so there is no edge to feel—and
        it stays completely still while another app has focus.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Opening it is a movement, not a cut.</h3><p>
        The command bar grows out of the resting island—starting at its exact
        size and shape, corners rounding out as it expands—and shrinks back into
        it when you dismiss. If you have reduce motion turned on, both of these
        are off entirely.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Search without leaving the island.</h3><p>
        Find tabs, Favorites, history and groups alongside search results. For
        search text, Enter opens the highlighted result. A strong match can come
        first; choose the search result showing your exact text when you want to
        search the web.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Open your whole session in one place.</h3><p>
        Open the island to switch tabs, navigate, favorite a page, start a
        private tab, or use the browser's commands—without moving the page
        underneath.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="island-personal-title">
  <div>
    <h2
      id="island-personal-title"
    >
      Get to a new page with one click.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>A Plus that puts you straight into the address field.</h3><p>
        The resting Island’s Plus opens one regular, ungrouped tab and focuses
        its address field. It sits beside the slash-command keycap. In
        vertical-tabs mode, use the rail’s New tab control instead.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Choose the icon you want to keep in your Dock.</h3><p>
        On macOS, Settings offers Sunrise and Sunrise Dark. Both app-icon
        choices are free; no Patron subscription is required.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Choose what a new tab looks like.</h3><p>
        Try a list of Favorites, local frequent sites, or launch standalone
        Mahjong from any footer. <a
          href="/support#start-page"
          data-track="feature_cta_click"
          data-feature="start-page"
          data-cta-position="related-feature"
          >Explore the four Start Page layouts</a
        >.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
